-- title:
--   An exponential bound for the number of local-cover rounds
-- statement:
--   Let $h\in\mathbb N$ and let $p_h$ be the local prime chosen by the construction. The prescribed greedy schedule length is
--
--   $$S_h=320(2h+1)\bigl(\log_2^{\mathrm{nat}}(p_h^2)+1\bigr),$$
--
--   where $\log_2^{\mathrm{nat}}$ is the natural-number floor logarithm. It satisfies
--
--   $$S_h\le2^{1029h+16}.$$
--
--   This explicit bound controls the number of retained schedule occurrences as part of the uniform local-cover resource estimate.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightLocalCoverMagnitude.lean#L43-L67

